# Mentorship codebase

Multi-tenant kernel for mentor–mentee programs. Program policy is data (`programs.policy`); long-running flows are durable sagas; the append-only domain event log is the spine. Full invariants and rejected alternatives: `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/decisions/`. Do not restate them — follow them.

## Layers (dependency direction is one-way; `pnpm deps:check`)

| Layer | Where | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kernel | `packages/core`, `events`, `db` | `core` imports only `zod` and node builtins. A type needed in two packages goes in `core`. |
| Orchestration | `packages/workflows` | Sagas read via `SagaResolvers` and mutate only by returning `Effect` descriptors. Never import `db` except the `postgres*.ts` seam (kept out of `index.ts`). |
| Primitives | `packages/ai`, `packages/primitives/{matching,nudge,session-intel,progress}` | `resolve → infer → gate → fallback`. Same postgres escape hatch: `src/postgres.ts` only. |
| Policy | `ProgramPolicySchema` in `core/policy.ts` | Runtime data. Never branch on a tenant name. |
| Surfaces | `packages/integrations/*`, `apps/{api,worker,web}` | One adapter per slot. `db` is reached only from `apps/api`, `apps/worker`, and the postgres seams above. |

`packages/testkit` is the in-memory stand-in. `pnpm test` needs no database and no model; Postgres tests need `docker compose up -d db`, `pnpm db:migrate`, and `DATABASE_URL`.

## How a session actually moves

`SessionLifecycle` (`workflows/session-lifecycle.ts`) is a discriminated union on `name`: `idle → proposing → scheduling → armed → awaiting_artifact → extracting → confirming → feedback → cooling`, or `paused`. Only `proposing` and `extracting` may call a model.

Effects do not return values. `create_calendar_event` emits `session.scheduled`; the saga waits for that event. Keys are `saga:{id}:{step}:{index}`. Every state has a `waitFor`, a `timeoutAt`, or `done`. Missing capabilities degrade in `createEffectRunner` (`effects.ts`) unless they change the flow (no transcription ⇒ never poll), which is a saga branch.

New event names go in `EVENT_NAMES` (`core/events.ts`) before use. New external tools implement a slot port in `core/capabilities.ts` (`conversation`, `dm`, `calendar`, `conferencing`, `transcript`, `document`, `sheet`, `dashboard`) and declare `AdapterCapabilities`.

## Constraints that look optional and are not

- Tenant reads and writes go through `withTenant(db, orgId, …)`. RLS uses `app.current_org`.
- Agreement is a table plus `resolveAgreement` (five outcomes). Buttons or a structured reply only — never prose. Negotiation caps at two rounds. Renudge once, then escalate.
- A `dm` that fails is retried once, then not sent and escalated (`dm_undeliverable`). It must never fall back to the joint thread.
- `feedback.sentiment` and a participant-attributed `signal` have no admin or program-lead branch in `authorize()` (`core/authorization.ts`).
- Notes are untrusted. Never splice them into a later prompt as instructions, and never let them authorize a send.
- `safeguarding` DMs `policy.safeguarding.contactMemberRef` via `notify_safeguarding` before any shared-doc or confirmation post.
- Scores and health are deterministic. The model drafts, explains, and prioritises. Extractions land `pending`; a timeout auto-confirm is marked unverified.
- Instants are UTC. `proposeSlots` returns `[]` when there is no mutual working hour.

## Conventions

Zod schema first, infer the type. Branded ids from `core/ids.ts`. Named exports, re-exported from each package `index.ts`. `import type` for type-only imports. Tests live in `src/__tests__/*.test.ts` and import via `@mentorship/*`. Comments record why, especially a rejected alternative.

`Dispatcher` queues events on purpose (inline delivery re-enters the engine). `SagaConflictError` is swallowed because the other writer won and the effect ledger makes the retry safe.

## Commands

`pnpm test` · `pnpm typecheck` · `pnpm deps:check` · `pnpm demo` (full session trace). Live Slack/Google: `docs/live-tenant-testing.md` before `pnpm seed:live-pair` or `pnpm serve:worker:live`. Web is Next.js at `apps/web` (`pnpm dev:web`, :3000), proxying `/api` to `apps/api` (:8787).
